=== PARITY (vs web ResultPanel.tsx) ===
  Web source (37 lines) is a pure presentational panel: props { title, data?, error?, idle?,
  idleMessage? }; hasData = data != null; stringifiedData = JSON.stringify(data, null, 2);
  body branch = error (rose) → hasData (<pre> + CopyButton) → idle (muted "No result yet");
  container tint = error ? bg-neon-red/5 : hasData ? bg-neon-green/5 : bg-white/[0.02].

  Data sources → "(none — pure presentational component)". The model binds through a push-based
    ResultPanelSource seam (P1/S8): the parent devtool harness pushes ResultPanelUpdate(outcome,
    connection, updatedAt). The view performs NO networking — trivially true and structurally enforced
    (the view only reads ResultPanelModel; the model only reads the source).
  Projection → ResultProjectionBuilder maps the exclusive outcome to a variant + render strings.
    JSONValue.prettyPrinted() is a byte-faithful port of JSON.stringify(data, null, 2): {} / [] collapse,
    members join with ",\n", 2-space indent, ECMAScript string escaping (named short escapes; \u00xx
    lowercase for other C0 controls; non-ASCII verbatim). Object key order is preserved (a hand-rolled
    order-preserving parser — Foundation JSONSerialization does NOT preserve key order). Verified by an
    executed harness against Node's reference output (28/28).
  Composition → header (title + CopyButton when hasData) over a state-driven body, tinted by variant
    the way the web container is (danger/success/glass). CopyButton parity: Copy ⇄ Copied toggle with a
    2s reset (web setTimeout(…, 2000)), reduce-motion-aware, VoiceOver-announced; writes via a clipboard
    seam (web navigator.clipboard.writeText → UIPasteboard/NSPasteboard).
  Shared components → web "@/components/ui". Renders over the REAL apps/apple design tokens + component
    library (Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSMotion / TSSkeleton), compiled against them in
    the typechecks below. The copy button + code block are built locally (the way OdometerReadout extends
    the tokens) to stay parallel-safe and host-compilable. Recharts→none / Leaflet→none.
  States (all render) → loading (skeleton code-block chrome) · empty/idle (muted "No result yet" or the
    caller's idleMessage, never a blank box) · error (danger message + Retry, the QueryError equivalent) ·
    stale (freshness chip + banner over the cached result) · offline (cached result + chip + banner) ·
    content (scrollable monospaced pretty JSON + CopyButton).
  i18n → the web source's only literal ('No result yet') resolves through the P1/S10 facade
    (devtools.resultPanel.idle); the CopyButton keys (common.copyButton.copy/copied) are present; the
    native chrome keys back loading/freshness/banners/retry/a11y. 13/13 keys referenced in code are
    PRESENT in ResultPanel.strings (parity-checked). No English literals in native code (title is a prop).
  a11y → the code block is one element labelled with the JSON; error/idle are combined elements; the copy
    button + retry have accessibilityLabels that track state; the panel is accessibilityElement(.contain);
    Dynamic Type via tokens; Reduce Motion gates the copy + variant transitions. Label content is unit-
    tested via ResultPanelAccessibility (pure seam).
  Telemetry → ResultPanelModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"ResultPanel") once → bridges shared
    Telemetry.track(.screenView) (P1/S11). Asserted by a spy in the executed harness.

